# The story map

The whole net has more than fifty concepts and nearly five hundred links, and
drawn in full it shows nothing. This map keeps the concepts that carry the
argument and the links between them that the cards declare. The eight
containers are the [north stars](north-stars.hmd). A concept sits in the star
that most of its claims fall under.

## The story

Read the map from the top.

1. **A notion, not a class.** "Strange loop" was fixed by examples and never
   defined, so the vault holds seven candidate definitions and a taxonomy in
   place of one answer.
2. **Levels, not cycles.** What the candidates share is a test: a level of
   description is crossed on the way round. Feedback, including the feedback
   loop of the documents themselves, goes round without crossing anything.
3. **Representation before reference.** Before a level can be crossed the
   system must hold a representation of itself. Gödel numbering is the exact
   case, a quine the minimal one, and the observer card the one this project
   can build.
4. **Limits from inside.** In the exact case the crossing has a provable
   consequence, the Gödel sentence and the incompleteness theorems, which hold
   there and are not a general fact about self-reference.
5. **A step from outside.** A theory gets past its limit by a step it cannot
   derive, the next stage of a progression. The documents get past theirs by a
   reviewed revision through a gate. Neither step needs a human; both need to
   be explicit.
6. **No operation alone.** That step is one turn of the reasoning cycle, in
   which induction, deduction, evaluation and revision are positions and none
   stands by itself.
7. **An operation is its signature.** The positions are operations, told apart
   by what goes in and what comes out.
8. **A candidate until checked.** A signature gives the form of a result. A
   typed transformation adds the evidence that makes it more than a candidate.

The card `knowledge-graph` is on the map as well. It describes this graph and
is a node of it.

## The map

```d2
direction: down

notion: A notion, not a class {
  definitions-of-strange-loop
  taxonomy-of-self-reference
}

levels: Levels, not cycles {
  strange-loop: strange-loop {
    style.bold: true
  }
  self-reference
  level-crossing
  object-and-meta-level
  feedback-loop
  hmd-feedback-loop
  knowledge-graph
}

representation: Representation before reference {
  godel-numbering
  quine
  observer-card-experiment
}

limits: Limits from inside {
  godel-sentence
  incompleteness-theorems
}

outside: A step from outside {
  reflection-progression
  human-in-the-loop
  render-integrate-execute
  revision
}

cycle: No operation alone {
  reasoning-cycle
}

signature: An operation is its signature {
  cognitive-operation
  induction
  deduction
  abstraction
  evaluation
}

checked: A candidate until checked {
  typed-transformation
}

notion.definitions-of-strange-loop -> levels.strange-loop: generalizes
notion.taxonomy-of-self-reference -> levels.self-reference: generalizes

levels.strange-loop -> levels.self-reference: is-a
levels.strange-loop -> levels.level-crossing: uses
levels.level-crossing -> levels.object-and-meta-level: uses
levels.strange-loop -> levels.feedback-loop: distinguished-from
levels.hmd-feedback-loop -> levels.feedback-loop: is-a
levels.knowledge-graph -> levels.self-reference: example-of
levels.knowledge-graph -> levels.strange-loop: distinguished-from

representation.godel-numbering -> levels.level-crossing: example-of
representation.quine -> levels.self-reference: is-a
representation.observer-card-experiment -> representation.godel-numbering: analogous-to
representation.observer-card-experiment -> levels.hmd-feedback-loop: instance-of

limits.godel-sentence -> representation.godel-numbering: uses
limits.godel-sentence -> levels.strange-loop: example-of
limits.godel-sentence -> limits.incompleteness-theorems: part-of

outside.reflection-progression -> limits.godel-sentence: uses
outside.reflection-progression -> limits.incompleteness-theorems: uses
outside.reflection-progression -> outside.human-in-the-loop: uses
outside.reflection-progression -> levels.hmd-feedback-loop: analogous-to
outside.render-integrate-execute -> outside.human-in-the-loop: uses
outside.render-integrate-execute -> outside.revision: is-a
outside.render-integrate-execute -> levels.hmd-feedback-loop: part-of
levels.knowledge-graph -> outside.revision: uses

outside.revision -> cycle.reasoning-cycle: part-of
cycle.reasoning-cycle -> levels.feedback-loop: is-a
cycle.reasoning-cycle -> levels.hmd-feedback-loop: generalizes

signature.induction -> cycle.reasoning-cycle: part-of
signature.deduction -> cycle.reasoning-cycle: part-of
signature.evaluation -> cycle.reasoning-cycle: part-of
signature.induction -> signature.deduction: contrasts
signature.induction -> signature.cognitive-operation: instance-of
signature.deduction -> signature.cognitive-operation: instance-of
signature.abstraction -> signature.cognitive-operation: instance-of
signature.abstraction -> levels.level-crossing: uses
signature.deduction -> limits.incompleteness-theorems: uses

signature.induction -> checked.typed-transformation: is-a
signature.deduction -> checked.typed-transformation: is-a
checked.typed-transformation -> signature.evaluation: uses
```

## How the map was made

- **The containers** are the north stars, and a star with no concept on the
  map would mean the story skips it. None is skipped.
- **The concepts** are twenty-five of the fifty-two that carry claims. A concept
  was kept when the story above cannot be told without naming it. That is a
  judgement, made once by reading, and it is the part of this map most open to
  dispute.
- **The arrows** are links the cards declare, with the relation they declare.
  No arrow was added to make the story run. Where two cards declare the same
  one-way relation in both directions (see the query
  [two-way links](../.hql/queries/two-way-links.hql)), neither direction was
  drawn.

Arrows that cross from one container to another are where two stars meet. The
query [star cover](../.hql/queries/star-cover.hql) lists every such meeting
under `overlaps`, with the cards the two stars share. The map draws the ones
the story passes through.

The map is written by hand and does not update itself. When claims or stars
change, the cover query says what moved, and the map has to be redrawn to
match.
